@@s066 The method in the exam room (4 hours)
@@s067 Read the 5 problems only for output and constraint. In the margin write what is optimised, on which structure, with which constraints.
@@s068 Assign the sure ones first: flow (two sets to pair) and traversal (reachability, distances).
@@s069 Eliminate: what remains is greedy, DP and NP-hard. Tell them apart with the trap pairs.
@@s070 <b>Test</b> the idea on Sample Input 1: if the output does not match, the classification is wrong, not the example.
@@s071 The observation that matters at the exam: the 5 problems are almost always variants of the same object. The text changes by one word and the paradigm changes completely. Read the goal and the constraints word by word.
